findings.finding:
The hop's parsing and matching rules are underspecified, which leaves real decisions to the executor:
- how to split `<remote>/<branch>` when the branch contains slashes (`origin/feature/x`);
- whether a `<remote>/<branch>` naming an unconfigured remote is ignored or an error;
- whether the full form `refs/remotes/origin/x` counts;
- how `origin/HEAD` is treated;
- whether 'differs from the base' compares ref names or resolved commits (e.g. base reached via refs/remotes/origin/HEAD, committed ref `origin/main`).
